12} \\) in the sequence defined by \\( S_1 = 1 \\), \\( S_2 = 1 \\), and \\( S_n = \\frac{S_{n-2} \\cdot S_{n-1}}{S_{n-2} + S_{n-1}} \\) for \\( n > 2 \\), we will compute the terms step by step.\n\nFirst, we calculate \\( S_3 \\):\n\\[\nS_3 = \\frac{S_1 \\cdot S_2}{S_1 + S_2} = \\frac{1 \\cdot 1}{1 + 1} = \\frac{1}{2}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\( S_4 \\):\n\\[\nS_4 = \\frac{S_2 \\cdot S_3}{S_2 + S_3} = \\frac{1 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}}{1 + \\frac{1}{2}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{2}}{\\frac{3}{2}} = \\frac{1}{3}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\( S_5 \\):\n\\[\nS_5 = \\frac{S_3 \\cdot S_4}{S_3 + S_4} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3}}{\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{6}}{\\frac{5}{6}} = \\frac{1}{5}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\( S_6 \\):\n\\[\nS_6 = \\frac{S_4 \\cdot S_5}{S_4 + S_5} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{5}}{\\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{1}{5}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{15}}{\\frac{8}{15}} = \\frac{1}{8}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\( S_7 \\):\n\\[\nS_7 = \\frac{S_5 \\cdot S_6}{S_5 + S_6} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{5} \\cdot \\frac{1}{8}}{\\frac{1}{5} + \\frac{1}{8}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{40}}{\\frac{13}{40}} = \\frac{1}{13}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\( S_8 \\):\n\\[\nS_8 = \\frac{S_6 \\cdot S_7}{S_6 + S_7} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{8} \\cdot \\frac{1}{13}}{\\frac{1}{8} + \\frac{1}{13}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{104}}{\\frac{21}{104}} = \\frac{1}{21}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\( S_9 \\):\n\\[\nS_9 = \\frac{S_7 \\cdot S_8}{S_7 + S_8} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{13} \\cdot \\frac{1}{21}}{\\frac{1}{13} + \\frac{1}{21}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{273}}{\\frac{34}{273}} = \\frac{1}{34}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\( S_{10} \\):\n\\[\nS_{10} = \\frac{S_8 \\cdot S_9}{S_8 + S_9} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{21} \\cdot \\frac{1}{34}}{\\frac{1}{21} + \\frac{1}{34}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{714}}{\\frac{55}{714}} = \\frac{1}{55}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\( S_{11} \\):\n\\[\nS_{11} = \\frac{S_9 \\cdot S_{10}}{S_9 + S_{10}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{34} \\cdot \\frac{1}{55}}{\\frac{1}{34} + \\frac{1}{55}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{1870}}{\\frac{89}{1870}} = \\frac{1}{89}\n\\]\n\nFinally, we calculate \\( S_{12} \\):\n\\[\nS_{12} = \\frac{S_{10} \\cdot S_{11}}{S_{10} + S_{11}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{55} \\cdot \\frac{1}{89}}{\\frac{1}{55} + \\frac{1}{89}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{4895}}{\\frac{144}{4895}} = \\frac{1}{144}\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( S_{12} \\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{144}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{1}{144}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"intermediate_algebra:426"}
